target: skills/review/review-loop/plan.py
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/plan.test.sh
expect: FAIL  a missing looper says the alarm is unavailable
why:    the plausible tidy-up — only ask looper for the alarm when the binary is there — makes a missing looper a silent Step 0 again: the alarm is skipped, nothing says so, and with --dry-run nothing else in plan.py mentions looper at all. A missing binary is a failure to surface like any other, which is why run() turning the OSError into an exit status is load-bearing here.
--- old
    rc, alarm, err = run([looper, "stats", "--alarm"], timeout=10)
--- new
    rc, alarm, err = (run([looper, "stats", "--alarm"], timeout=10)
                      if os.access(looper, os.X_OK) else (0, "", ""))
